%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: ef4685dce134df8409bc6416fb74028e, type: 3}
  m_Name: ViCSIDialogueCatalog
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::ViCSIDialogueCatalog
  dialogueConfirmationSeconds: 2.75
  dialogueGuidanceSeconds: 4
  dialogueWarningSeconds: 5
  dialogueErrorSeconds: 5
  tooltipSeconds: 2
  tooltipImportantSeconds: 2.75
  skipProtectionSeconds: 0.25
  entries:
  - id: narr-mission-scene-start-1
    category: 0
    type: 0
    speaker: 
    text: You've got several accounts to work with, but don't let them decide the
      case for you. Start by documenting the room, John and anything that might be
      connected. Then see what the scene actually supports.
    duration: 0
    priority: 1
    skippable: 1
    replaceBehavior: 0
    notes: First professor line after the First Responder turnover (event 'mission-scene-start',
      priority 100). It directs the student to document the scene before weighing
      statements.
  - id: narr-beat-1-initial-briefing-1
    category: 0
    type: 0
    speaker: 
    text: Paul, Peter and the vendor give you somewhere to start. Keep track of what
      each person says, and check it against what you find here.
    duration: 8
    priority: 1
    skippable: 1
    replaceBehavior: 0
    notes: Consolidated professor guidance for event 'beat-1-initial-briefing'. The
      First Responder has already supplied the known scene and witness facts.
  - id: evidence-status-discovered
    category: 0
    type: 1
    speaker: 
    text: '{0} {1} been discovered.'
    duration: 0
    priority: 0
    skippable: 1
    replaceBehavior: 2
    notes: '{0} = evidence display name, {1} = ''has'' or ''have'' (chosen automatically
      from the name).'
  - id: prompt-attic-ladder
    category: 0
    type: 1
    speaker: 
    text: '[B] Toggle Attic Ladder'
    duration: 0
    priority: 1
    skippable: 1
    replaceBehavior: 2
    notes: Standing prompt near the attic ladder lever.
  - id: prompt-furniture-open
    category: 0
    type: 1
    speaker: 
    text: '[Trigger] Open'
    duration: 0
    priority: 1
    skippable: 1
    replaceBehavior: 2
    notes: Standing prompt at a closed drawer/cabinet/door.
  - id: prompt-furniture-close
    category: 0
    type: 1
    speaker: 
    text: '[Trigger] Close'
    duration: 0
    priority: 1
    skippable: 1
    replaceBehavior: 2
    notes: Standing prompt at an open drawer/cabinet/door.
  - id: FR_TURNOVER_01
    category: 0
    type: 0
    speaker: First Responder
    text: We've kept access under control since we arrived, and the house is still
      cordoned off. John was found on the floor inside with what looks like a stab
      wound. We're treating this as a suspected violent death.
    duration: 18
    priority: 1
    skippable: 1
    replaceBehavior: 0
    notes: FR to IOC turnover line 1/4. Preliminary information only; no forensic
      interpretation.
  - id: FR_TURNOVER_02
    category: 0
    type: 0
    speaker: First Responder
    text: The nearby vendor is the one who called us after finding John. We were
      told John had been drinking here with his brother Paul and a friend named Peter.
      The vendor says he saw Peter leave around two in the morning, looking nervous
      or sick. He did not witness the attack.
    duration: 22
    priority: 1
    skippable: 1
    replaceBehavior: 0
    notes: FR to IOC turnover line 2/4. Preliminary information only; no forensic
      interpretation.
  - id: FR_TURNOVER_03
    category: 0
    type: 0
    speaker: First Responder
    text: We've kept the scene as we found it after the initial response; no forensic
      work has been done yet. I didn't witness the attack. What we've heard about
      the drinking and Peter leaving still needs checking.
    duration: 18
    priority: 1
    skippable: 1
    replaceBehavior: 0
    notes: FR to IOC turnover line 3/4. Preliminary information only; no forensic
      interpretation.
  - id: FR_TURNOVER_04
    category: 0
    type: 0
    speaker: First Responder
    text: Here's the completed CSI Form 1, the First Responder's Report, with the
      information we've gathered. The scene is yours now. We'll keep the cordon secure
      and help where you need us.
    duration: 18
    priority: 1
    skippable: 1
    replaceBehavior: 0
    notes: FR to IOC turnover line 4/4. Preliminary information only; no forensic
      interpretation.
  - id: statement-paul-evening
    category: 0
    type: 0
    speaker: Paul
    text: Yeah, we were drinking earlier. John and I argued about some family stuff,
      but that wasn't unusual for us. I left around midnight; Peter was still there
      when I went home.
    duration: 0
    priority: 1
    skippable: 1
    replaceBehavior: 0
    notes: Central statement catalog for later interview or case-file presentation.
      It is not triggered by Phase 1 gameplay.
  - id: statement-paul-alibi
    category: 0
    type: 0
    speaker: Paul
    text: I went straight home. I didn't come back after that.
    duration: 0
    priority: 1
    skippable: 1
    replaceBehavior: 0
    notes: Central Paul follow-up statement for later use. Not wired to new gameplay
      in Phase 1.
  - id: statement-paul-knife
    category: 0
    type: 0
    speaker: Paul
    text: I've used that knife before. It's from John's kitchen. Finding my print
      on it doesn't mean I used it on him.
    duration: 0
    priority: 1
    skippable: 1
    replaceBehavior: 0
    notes: Prepared confrontation line for later use. Not triggered by Phase 1 gameplay.
  - id: statement-peter-timeline
    category: 0
    type: 0
    speaker: Peter
    text: I stayed a while after Paul left, but then I started feeling sick. I left
      around two in the morning. John was still awake when I walked out.
    duration: 0
    priority: 1
    skippable: 1
    replaceBehavior: 0
    notes: Central Peter statement for later interview or case-file presentation.
      It is not triggered by Phase 1 gameplay.
  - id: statement-peter-appearance
    category: 0
    type: 0
    speaker: Peter
    text: I probably did look bad. I'd been drinking and I felt like I was going
      to throw up. I just wanted to get home.
    duration: 0
    priority: 1
    skippable: 1
    replaceBehavior: 0
    notes: Central Peter follow-up statement for later use. Not wired to new gameplay
      in Phase 1.
  - id: statement-peter-money
    category: 0
    type: 0
    speaker: Peter
    text: We'd argued about money before, sure. I was frustrated with him, but I
      did not hurt him.
    duration: 0
    priority: 1
    skippable: 1
    replaceBehavior: 0
    notes: Central Peter follow-up statement for later use. Not wired to new gameplay
      in Phase 1.
  - id: statement-vendor-peter-leaving
    category: 0
    type: 0
    speaker: Vendor
    text: I was still up when I saw Peter coming out of John's place, sometime around
      two. He didn't look right. Nervous, or maybe sick; I couldn't really tell.
    duration: 0
    priority: 1
    skippable: 1
    replaceBehavior: 0
    notes: Central reporting-witness statement for later interview or case-file presentation.
      It is not triggered by Phase 1 gameplay.
  - id: statement-vendor-discovery
    category: 0
    type: 0
    speaker: Vendor
    text: I came back later to check on John. He wasn't answering, so I went inside
      and found him on the floor. I called the police right away.
    duration: 0
    priority: 1
    skippable: 1
    replaceBehavior: 0
    notes: Central reporting-witness discovery statement for later use. Not wired
      to new gameplay in Phase 1.
  - id: statement-vendor-limitation
    category: 0
    type: 0
    speaker: Vendor
    text: I didn't see what happened inside. All I saw then was Peter leaving.
    duration: 0
    priority: 1
    skippable: 1
    replaceBehavior: 0
    notes: Central reporting-witness limitation statement for later use. Not wired
      to new gameplay in Phase 1.
  - id: vendor-placeholder-label
    category: 0
    type: 1
    speaker: 
    text: Vendor
    duration: 0
    priority: 1
    skippable: 1
    replaceBehavior: 0
    notes: Physical vendor placeholder name label.
  - id: prompt-talk-vendor
    category: 0
    type: 1
    speaker: 
    text: Vendor - [A] Talk
    duration: 0
    priority: 1
    skippable: 1
    replaceBehavior: 0
    notes: Physical vendor interaction prompt; opens the existing follow-up panel.
  - id: vendor-followup-heading
    category: 0
    type: 0
    speaker: Vendor
    text: Vendor follow-up / Statements
    duration: 0
    priority: 1
    skippable: 1
    replaceBehavior: 0
    notes: Session-local vendor follow-up; available during SOCO investigation. Discovery
      is required for the new board fact.
  - id: vendor-followup-anyone-else
    category: 0
    type: 0
    speaker: Investigator
    text: Did you see anyone else near John's house besides Peter?
    duration: 0
    priority: 1
    skippable: 1
    replaceBehavior: 0
    notes: Session-local vendor follow-up; available during SOCO investigation. Discovery
      is required for the new board fact.
  - id: statement-vendor-paul-3am
    category: 0
    type: 0
    speaker: Vendor
    text: Now that you mention it, I remember seeing Paul near John's house around
      three in the morning. I didn't see where he went after that.
    duration: 0
    priority: 1
    skippable: 1
    replaceBehavior: 0
    notes: Session-local vendor follow-up; available during SOCO investigation. Discovery
      is required for the new board fact.
  - id: vendor-paul-3am-summary
    category: 0
    type: 0
    speaker: Vendor
    text: Vendor saw Paul near John's house around 3:00 AM.
    duration: 0
    priority: 1
    skippable: 1
    replaceBehavior: 0
    notes: Session-local vendor follow-up; available during SOCO investigation. Discovery
      is required for the new board fact.
  - id: vendor-paul-3am-detail
    category: 0
    type: 0
    speaker: Vendor
    text: The vendor remembers seeing Paul walking near John's house sometime around
      3:00 AM. He recognized Paul but did not see where Paul went afterward. He did
      not see Paul enter the house and did not witness the attack. This observation
      does not establish who attacked John.
    duration: 0
    priority: 1
    skippable: 1
    replaceBehavior: 0
    notes: Session-local vendor follow-up; available during SOCO investigation. Discovery
      is required for the new board fact.
  - id: prompt-talk-first-responder
    category: 0
    type: 1
    speaker: 
    text: '[A] Receive scene turnover'
    duration: 0
    priority: 1
    skippable: 1
    replaceBehavior: 2
    notes: FIRST RESPONDER standing prompt while the player is within the NPC's interaction
      radius and the scene has not been turned over yet.
  - id: csi-form-1-received
    category: 0
    type: 1
    speaker: 
    text: 'CSI Form 1 received and added to case records.

      Conduct an initial
      assessment of the scene.'
    duration: 6
    priority: 0
    skippable: 1
    replaceBehavior: 0
    notes: Procedural FR to IOC document receipt and broad next objective; no form-entry
      UI.
  - id: fr-early-entry-warning
    category: 0
    type: 1
    speaker: 
    text: Speak with the First Responder before entering the scene.
    duration: 0
    priority: 2
    skippable: 1
    replaceBehavior: 0
    notes: FIRST RESPONDER warning shown by SceneCordon when the player walks into
      the scene before turnover. Nothing starts.
  - id: photo-point-exterior-establishing
    category: 1
    type: 1
    speaker: 
    text: Begin by documenting the scene from outside before entering. Photograph
      the whole house.
    duration: 3.5
    priority: 1
    skippable: 1
    replaceBehavior: 2
    notes: Instruction when 'Exterior establishing shot' (photo point scene-exterior-establishing,
      step 10) becomes the active view.
  - id: photo-point-entrance-approach
    category: 1
    type: 1
    speaker: 
    text: Photograph the porch and front doorway before moving inside.
    duration: 3.5
    priority: 1
    skippable: 1
    replaceBehavior: 2
    notes: Instruction when 'Entrance and approach' (photo point scene-entrance-approach,
      step 20) becomes the active view.
  - id: photo-point-interior-from-entrance
    category: 1
    type: 1
    speaker: 
    text: Step inside. Capture an overall view before focusing on individual items.
    duration: 3.5
    priority: 1
    skippable: 1
    replaceBehavior: 2
    notes: Instruction when 'Interior overall from the entrance' (photo point scene-interior-from-entrance,
      step 30) becomes the active view.
  - id: photo-point-interior-left
    category: 1
    type: 1
    speaker: 
    text: Photograph the living area from the left side to record the furniture layout.
    duration: 3.5
    priority: 1
    skippable: 1
    replaceBehavior: 2
    notes: Instruction when 'Interior overall, left side' (photo point scene-interior-left,
      step 40) becomes the active view.
  - id: photo-point-interior-right
    category: 1
    type: 1
    speaker: 
    text: Photograph the living area from the opposite side to complete its overall
      coverage.
    duration: 3.5
    priority: 1
    skippable: 1
    replaceBehavior: 2
    notes: Instruction when 'Interior overall, right side' (photo point scene-interior-right,
      step 50) becomes the active view.
  - id: photo-point-body-in-scene
    category: 1
    type: 1
    speaker: 
    text: Enter the rear ground-floor kitchen. Photograph John's body in its surroundings.
    duration: 3.5
    priority: 1
    skippable: 1
    replaceBehavior: 2
    notes: Instruction when 'Victim within the scene' (photo point scene-body-in-scene,
      step 60) becomes the active view.
  - id: photo-point-stair-incident-area
    category: 1
    type: 1
    speaker: 
    text: Photograph the rear kitchen to show the counters, the body and the floor
      around the evidence.
    duration: 3.5
    priority: 1
    skippable: 1
    replaceBehavior: 2
    notes: Instruction when 'Kitchen and incident area' (photo point scene-stair-incident-area,
      step 70 - id kept from when it faced the stairs) becomes the active view.
  - id: photo-zone-entered
    category: 1
    type: 1
    speaker: 
    text: You're in position. Equip the camera and press [X] then aim at the scene.
    duration: 3.5
    priority: 1
    skippable: 1
    replaceBehavior: 2
    notes: Player stepped into the active photo point's marked circle. {0} = the
      view's name.
  - id: evidence-step-photograph-first
    category: 1
    type: 0
    speaker: 
    text: Photograph this item before continuing so its original position and condition
      are documented before it is disturbed.
    duration: 0
    priority: 3
    skippable: 1
    replaceBehavior: 3
    notes: 'Refusal: the item needs its first (raw) photograph.'
  - id: evidence-step-final-photo-first
    category: 1
    type: 0
    speaker: 
    text: Take the final photograph before continuing so the evidence and its identifying
      marker are documented together.
    duration: 0
    priority: 3
    skippable: 1
    replaceBehavior: 3
    notes: 'Refusal: the final (with-marker) photograph comes next.'
  - id: photo-out-of-sequence
    category: 1
    type: 0
    speaker: 
    text: Document the earlier scene view first.
    duration: 0
    priority: 2
    skippable: 1
    replaceBehavior: 3
    notes: Photo taken for a later view while an earlier required view is still open.
  - id: photo-wrong-position
    category: 1
    type: 0
    speaker: 
    text: Stand inside the marked area to take this photo.
    duration: 0
    priority: 2
    skippable: 1
    replaceBehavior: 3
    notes: Shutter pressed outside the active point's circle.
  - id: photo-wrong-angle
    category: 1
    type: 0
    speaker: 
    text: Aim toward the required scene area.
    duration: 0
    priority: 2
    skippable: 1
    replaceBehavior: 3
    notes: Shutter pressed inside the circle but facing the wrong way.
  - id: photo-scene-complete
    category: 1
    type: 0
    speaker: 
    text: Scene documentation complete. You may continue with detailed investigation.
    duration: 0
    priority: 0
    skippable: 1
    replaceBehavior: 0
    notes: All required overall scene views documented - evidence work unlocks.
  - id: step-scene-photos-before-evidence-photos
    category: 1
    type: 0
    speaker: 
    text: Document the overall scene before detailed evidence photographs so each
      item can be reviewed in its original scene context.
    duration: 0
    priority: 2
    skippable: 1
    replaceBehavior: 3
    notes: 'Procedure-order rule on the evidence items: refusal reason (Block) or
      camera warning (Warn). Also written to the session log as the expected prerequisite
      when the rule has none.'
  - id: step-scene-photos-before-chalk
    category: 1
    type: 0
    speaker: 
    text: Complete overall scene photography before marking positions so the scene
      is documented before anything is added or altered.
    duration: 0
    priority: 2
    skippable: 1
    replaceBehavior: 3
    notes: 'Procedure-order rule on the evidence items: refusal reason (Block) or
      camera warning (Warn). Also written to the session log as the expected prerequisite
      when the rule has none.'
  - id: step-scene-photos-before-markers
    category: 1
    type: 0
    speaker: 
    text: Complete overall scene photography before placing markers so the original
      appearance of the scene is preserved.
    duration: 0
    priority: 2
    skippable: 1
    replaceBehavior: 3
    notes: 'Procedure-order rule on the evidence items: refusal reason (Block) or
      camera warning (Warn). Also written to the session log as the expected prerequisite
      when the rule has none.'
  - id: step-scene-photos-before-sampling
    category: 1
    type: 0
    speaker: 
    text: Document the overall scene before biological sampling so the material and
      its surroundings are recorded before collection.
    duration: 0
    priority: 2
    skippable: 1
    replaceBehavior: 3
    notes: 'Procedure-order rule on the evidence items: refusal reason (Block) or
      camera warning (Warn). Also written to the session log as the expected prerequisite
      when the rule has none.'
  - id: step-scene-photos-before-fingerprints
    category: 1
    type: 0
    speaker: 
    text: Complete overall scene photography before fingerprint processing so the
      original condition is documented before treatment.
    duration: 0
    priority: 2
    skippable: 1
    replaceBehavior: 3
    notes: 'Procedure-order rule on the evidence items: refusal reason (Block) or
      camera warning (Warn). Also written to the session log as the expected prerequisite
      when the rule has none.'
  - id: step-scene-photos-before-collection
    category: 1
    type: 0
    speaker: 
    text: Complete overall scene photography before collection so the original positions
      and condition of items are preserved in the record.
    duration: 0
    priority: 2
    skippable: 1
    replaceBehavior: 3
    notes: 'Procedure-order rule on the evidence items: refusal reason (Block) or
      camera warning (Warn). Also written to the session log as the expected prerequisite
      when the rule has none.'
  - id: evidence-status-photographed
    category: 1
    type: 1
    speaker: 
    text: '{0} {1} been photographed.'
    duration: 0
    priority: 0
    skippable: 1
    replaceBehavior: 2
    notes: '{0} = evidence display name, {1} = ''has'' or ''have'' (chosen automatically
      from the name). First (raw) evidence photograph.'
  - id: evidence-status-final-photographed
    category: 1
    type: 1
    speaker: 
    text: '{0} {1} been photographed.'
    duration: 0
    priority: 0
    skippable: 1
    replaceBehavior: 2
    notes: '{0} = evidence display name, {1} = ''has'' or ''have'' (chosen automatically
      from the name). Final photograph (with marker).'
  - id: photo-view-unnamed
    category: 1
    type: 1
    speaker: 
    text: this view
    duration: 0
    priority: 1
    skippable: 1
    replaceBehavior: 2
    notes: Name used in photo-zone-entered when a photo point has no display name.
  - id: narr-mission-body-examination-1
    category: 2
    type: 0
    speaker: 
    text: Complete John's final photograph with Body Marker A in frame, then measure
      his position and record the findings before removal.
    duration: 6.8
    priority: 1
    skippable: 1
    replaceBehavior: 0
    notes: Narrative line 1/1 of event 'mission-body-examination' (was Pool_MissionBodyExam.asset).
  - id: narr-mission-body-wound-result-1
    category: 2
    type: 0
    speaker: 
    text: The wound looks consistent with a sharp-edged object. Compare it with the
      possible weapons you've documented, and see what fits.
    duration: 7
    priority: 1
    skippable: 1
    replaceBehavior: 0
    notes: Narrative line 1/1 of event 'mission-body-wound-result' (was Pool_MissionBodyWoundResult.asset).
  - id: narr-beat-2-body-doubt-1
    category: 2
    type: 0
    speaker: 
    text: 'Recorder: The wound''s narrow and deep. That fits an injury from a sharp-edged
      object.'
    duration: 5.7
    priority: 1
    skippable: 1
    replaceBehavior: 0
    notes: Narrative line 1/2 of event 'beat-2-body-doubt' (was DialoguePool_Beat2_BodyDoubt.asset).
  - id: narr-beat-2-body-doubt-2
    category: 2
    type: 0
    speaker: 
    text: 'Recorder: Let''s record what the wound tells us, then see how it fits
      with the rest of the scene.'
    duration: 5.8
    priority: 1
    skippable: 1
    replaceBehavior: 0
    notes: Narrative line 2/2 of event 'beat-2-body-doubt' (was DialoguePool_Beat2_BodyDoubt.asset).
  - id: evidence-examined-in-place
    category: 2
    type: 0
    speaker: 
    text: This evidence is examined in place and cannot be collected or sealed.
    duration: 0
    priority: 3
    skippable: 1
    replaceBehavior: 3
    notes: 'Refusal: trying to bag/seal the body.'
  - id: narr-mission-knife-fingerprint-before-1
    category: 3
    type: 0
    speaker: 
    text: The knife may help us find out who handled it. Get it documented, then
      sample the blood on the blade before dusting the handle for prints.
    duration: 7
    priority: 1
    skippable: 1
    replaceBehavior: 0
    notes: Narrative line 1/1 of event 'mission-knife-fingerprint-before' (was Pool_MissionKnifeBefore.asset).
  - id: narr-beat-3-knife-wound-match-1
    category: 3
    type: 0
    speaker: 
    text: 'Recorder: The blade''s dimensions match the wound profile.'
    duration: 4.8
    priority: 1
    skippable: 1
    replaceBehavior: 0
    notes: Narrative line 1/2 of event 'beat-3-knife-wound-match' (was DialoguePool_Beat3_KnifeWound.asset).
  - id: narr-beat-3-knife-wound-match-2
    category: 3
    type: 0
    speaker: 
    text: 'Recorder: This knife could be the weapon. Let''s see whether the other
      findings support that.'
    duration: 5.6
    priority: 1
    skippable: 1
    replaceBehavior: 0
    notes: Narrative line 2/2 of event 'beat-3-knife-wound-match' (was DialoguePool_Beat3_KnifeWound.asset).
  - id: team-evidence-014-logged-1
    category: 3
    type: 0
    speaker: 
    text: 'Dispatch: Got the knife''s dimensions and its position relative to the
      counter.'
    duration: 5.5
    priority: 1
    skippable: 1
    replaceBehavior: 0
    notes: Teammate line 1/2 for STCS trigger 'evidence_014_logged' (was DialoguePool_Evidence014Photographed.asset).
  - id: team-evidence-014-logged-2
    category: 3
    type: 0
    speaker: 
    text: 'Recorder: Copy. I''ve added the kitchen knife to the evidence log.'
    duration: 5.6
    priority: 1
    skippable: 1
    replaceBehavior: 0
    notes: Teammate line 2/2 for STCS trigger 'evidence_014_logged' (was DialoguePool_Evidence014Photographed.asset).
  - id: team-evidence-014-photographed-1
    category: 3
    type: 0
    speaker: 
    text: 'Dispatch: We''ve got a clear photo of the knife before it''s touched.'
    duration: 5.2
    priority: 1
    skippable: 1
    replaceBehavior: 0
    notes: Teammate line 1/1 for STCS trigger 'evidence_014_photographed' (was DialoguePool_Evidence014Photographed_Raw.asset).
  - id: team-evidence-014-chalk-marked-1
    category: 3
    type: 0
    speaker: 
    text: 'Dispatch: The knife''s position is outlined. We can place the marker there.'
    duration: 6
    priority: 1
    skippable: 1
    replaceBehavior: 0
    notes: Teammate line 1/1 for STCS trigger 'evidence_014_chalk_marked' (was DialoguePool_Evidence014ChalkMarked.asset).
  - id: team-evidence-014-collected-1
    category: 3
    type: 0
    speaker: 
    text: 'Dispatch: Copy, the knife''s bagged. Keep it steady.'
    duration: 4.6
    priority: 1
    skippable: 1
    replaceBehavior: 0
    notes: Teammate line 1/1 for STCS trigger 'evidence_014_collected' (was DialoguePool_Evidence014Collected.asset).
  - id: team-evidence-014-sealed-1
    category: 3
    type: 0
    speaker: 
    text: 'Recorder: The bag''s sealed. We''ll keep the custody record with it.'
    duration: 4.8
    priority: 1
    skippable: 1
    replaceBehavior: 0
